<<<
inure, enure. Both the connexion between the verb’s different senses (The poor, inured to drudgery & disiress; The cessions of land enured to the benefit of Georgia), & its derivation,
===
**inure, enure.** Both the connexion between the verb's different senses (*The poor, inured to drudgery & distress*; *The cessions of land enured to the benefit of Georgia*), & its derivation,
>>>

<<<
The origin is the obsolete noun ure (We will never enact, put in ure, promulge, or execute, any new canons), which is from French œuvre, which is from Latin opera work.
===
The origin is the obsolete noun *ure* (*We will never enact, put in ure, promulge, or execute, any new canons*), which is from French *œuvre*, which is from Latin *opera* work.
>>>

<<<
Variant spellings are therefore unnecessary, & in- is preferred by the OED. invade makes -dable; see MUTE E. invalid. The word meaning not valid is pronounced invi/lid.
===
Variant spellings are therefore unnecessary, & *in-* is preferred by the OED.

**invade** makes *-dable*; see ^^MUTE E^^.

**invalid.** The word meaning not valid is pronounced ĭnvă'lĭd.
